^SAMPLE = GSM4824487
!Sample_title = CTRL
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM4824487
!Sample_status = Public on Aug 04 2026
!Sample_submission_date = Oct 08 2020
!Sample_last_update_date = Aug 04 2026
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = human induced pluripotent stem cells, primary human cholangiocytes, human immortalised stellate cells line
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: control sample
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = time point: NA
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = disease state: Healthy
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = 3D co-cultures were treated with free fatty acids (Oleic Acid or Palmitic Acid) for 24hrs up to 1week.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = hIPSC-derived hepatocytes, macrophages, cholangiocytes and stellate cells were seeded at physiologic ratio and grown in a collagen based 3D system for up to 1week.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = The single cell solution from each sample was loaded onto the Chromium single cell controller by 10X genomics, a droplet-based single cell capture platform.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Single cells were lysed and tagged by a bead containing unique molecular identifiers (UMIs), and encapsulated in an oil droplet.; this emulsion was amplified through reverse-transcription, and subsequent library preparation was performed following the 10X Genomics manual instructions.
!Sample_data_processing = Quality of fastq files was assessed with FastQC v0.11.3, MultiQC v1.8.
!Sample_data_processing = Alignment and protein-coding gene quantification was performed using 10x cellranger v3.1.0
!Sample_data_processing = Normalization of expression was levels was performed with sctransform (Hafemeister and Satija, 2019)
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCh38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: csv files of raw and post-QC normalized expression levels
